      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Unkempt Woods [zone=1326]\n**Who:**\n- Wegadas [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Elaborate Peace Offering [item=148422]\n- Jeweler's Glass [item=148421]\n- Mysterious Signet [item=148420]\n- Thunder Chum [item=148419]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Rallosian Darksergeant [npc=59446]\n- Rallosian Deathsergeant [npc=59447]\n- Rallosian Warsergeant [npc=59448]\n- a Rallosian attacker [npc=59769]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Unkempt Woods (15 Points) [quest=12659]\n- The Blades of My Enemy [quest=12856]\n**Era:** | !Laurion's Song\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Dec 22 02:35:25 2023\nModified: Tue Jan 30 17:59:05 2024 | | **Laurion's Song Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisites: The Blades of My Enemy [quest=12856]**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this solo task from Wegadas [npc=59454] in Unkempt Woods. You can find Wegadas at the far southeastern corner of the zone at /way -2236, -2976, -300 He is on the find tool as well CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Wegadas'\nWegadas says, 'Oh, guests! Please, please, come and stay awhile!' He waves the adventurer closer. 'Welcome to our humble settlement. I would offer you some of the best Elddar hospitality, but I'm afraid I am woefully underprepared for it. I am low on [supplies], you see. But... BUT... I can share abundant stories.''\nYou say, 'I can find some supplies for you.'\nWegadas says, 'Oh no, I wouldn't do that to you.' He emphatically shakes his head. 'You are guests here among us, it would be rather rude of me to send you on an [errand].'\nYou say, 'No, I insist. I don't mind an errand.'\nWegadas says, 'You are very insistent, indeed.' He shakes his head in resignation and smiles to the adventurer. 'Well, if I was to honor you with our hospitality, I would recommend one of the local fish, the Thunder Chum. It is exquisite. It can be fished along the southern end of the river. But... no more than that. For the love of Tunare, no more than that! It would be the opposite of hospitable if I made you work for it. If you can [get one], I can cook it up for you in our traditional style.'\nYou say, 'Yes, I can get one.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Gift of Fish'.\nWegadas says, 'You will love it, I assure you. Remember, one Thunder Chum, and I'll be right here waiting for you when you get back.'\n\n---\n\nWegadas is a young druid intent on showing hospitality to the adventurers on their visit to the Elddar village. As he doesn't have the appropriate fish for the occasion, he's asked if you don't mind getting it and he'll prepare it. Nothing is ever so easy in the Unkempt Woods.\nWegadas mentioned the fish can be fished from the southern end of the river. That should be near the aviaks.\n1\\. Head to the southern end of the Unkempt river, and prepare to fish 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nOnce you are at the southern end of the river, equipping a fishing pole will immediately spawn a Rallosian attacker so be ready. Killing the Rallosian attacker will count for others in the group so you don't have to do this step for each person in the group.\n2\\. Defend yourself, and kill the Rallosian attacker 0/1 Unkempt Woods\n3\\. Loot a Mysterious Signet 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nThe Rallosian attacker drops this, loot it.\n4\\. Give Wegadas the Thunder Chum 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou offered 1 Thunder Chum to Wegadas.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'This is perfect! Let me start the preparation of this fine specimen.'\nYou complete the trade with Wegadas.\n5\\. Check in with Wegads regarding what occurred 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou say, 'Hail, Wegadas'\nWegadas says, 'Wait, do you mean there's more to the [situation]?'\nYou say, 'The situation is I was ambushed by a Rallosian.'\nWegadas says, 'In the south? Are you sure?' He pauses in his preparation of the fish. 'Was there anything notable about [the Rallosian]?''\nYou say, 'The Rallosian was a shaman and had a strange signet on her.'\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'Oh really...' He cleans off his hands, and puts his full attention on the adventurer. 'Can you tell me more of this [signet]?''\nYou say, 'The signet has some strange markings on it.'\nWegadas says, 'Oh, do tell. Could you tell me of the markings? I can spare a [magnifying glass] if it helps.'\nYou say, 'Yes, please, I could use a magnifying glass.'\nWegadas says, 'Here you go. Don't lose it. I only have so many of them!'\n6\\. Study the inscribed imagery on the signet 0/5 Unkempt Woods\nRight click the Jeweler's Glass he gave you 5 times.\nThe first mark appears as a rough symbol of Drinal. It may be of the moon of Norrath, or of the demigod, but it is difficult to tell in this Age.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nYou begin casting Examine Signet.\nThe second mark appears as though it was worn down over time. Just how old is this signet even in this time period?\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nYou begin casting Examine Signet.\nThe third mark appears as a bear head, the visual clear as day.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nYou begin casting Examine Signet.\nThe fourth mark is partially chipped away, but appears as a general symbol of nature.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nYou begin casting Examine Signet.\nThe fifth and final mark is partially chipped away, but appears as an ancient symbol of Tunare, the Mother of All. It's not like a Rallosian to hold an artifact of Tunare...\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\n7\\. Give the Mysterious Signet to Wegadas 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou offered 1 Mysterious Signet to Wegadas.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'This signet is... Amazing!'\nYou complete the trade with Wegadas.\n8\\. Give the Jeweler's Glass to Wegadas 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou offered 1 Jeweler's Glass to Wegadas.\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'This is much appreciated. Thank you for giving it back.'\nYou complete the trade with Wegadas.\n9\\. Discuss the Signet with Wegadas 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou say, 'Hail, Wegadas'\nWegadas says, 'This signet, based off of what you told me, and the materials it's made from, may...' He pauses as he tries to work through the logic of it all. 'It may belong to the mythical [Gihjna]. I have never seen them, but I assure you that they would not be allied with the Rallosians.'\nYou say, 'What are the Gihjna?'\nWegadas says, 'The Gihjna are great bear spirits native to this land, and the lands between the lands, and the lands beyond the lands. They and the Lujien, the great wolf spirits, were here before, and they will be here after. At least, that's what the stories say; until now, until this signet, I haven't taken much [faith] in it.'\nYou say, 'I am sorry if this discovery has shaken your faith.'\nWegadas says, 'Don't be. Don't apologize. If we're not all on a path of growth, then what are we doing with ourselves?' Shaking his head slowly, he reexamines the signet in his hand. 'I have an idea. If, and I mean IF, the Gihjna are here among us, and they have had a run-in with the Rallosians, we must [show that] we are not of the same heart as our invaders. We wish to share this land in harmony...'\nYou say, 'How do we show that?'\nWegadas says, 'I am not sure which is the best method, honestly. Should we perform a show of force to let them know that we do not appreciate the bloodthirsty invaders here? Should we offer a peace offering to show them our friendship? Should we try [both]? I am not sure if that would be too heavy-handed.'\nYou say, 'Perhaps both may be best.'\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'I suppose you're right. It's the most likely to get their attention, and the attacks on the Rallosians can only help our soldiers with pushing the invaders back.' He turns his attention towards the Thunder Chum. 'I hope you don't mind, but I will prepare this for the offering while you work your magic against the Rallosians.'\n10\\. Kill 3 Rallosian leaders 0/3 Unkempt Woods\nAny number of Rallosian Darksergeant's, Deathsergeant's, and Warsergeant's count for this step.\nRares do not count towards this step\n11\\. Kill 10 Rallosians 0/10 Unkempt Woods\nAny \"a Rallosian \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" will work for this step.\nRares and Rallosian \\_\\_\\_sergeants do not count towards this step\n12\\. Check in with Wegadas again 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou say, 'Hail, Wegadas'\nYou have been given: Elaborate Peace Offering\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'You have done an immense service to the Elddar people. Please know that even if this comes down to nothing, that you have helped us beyond measure. Oh! On that note...' From behind himself, he pulls out an urn, but the contents within smell savory and tantalize the senses. 'Take this to the caverns to the north. The dwarves are mining it out, but it is also the closest we have to touching the Valley of the Dawn. If they are there, they will see it and accept it.'\n13\\. Take a Peace Offering to the Dwarven tunnels 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nAt /way 2859, -3573, -429 in the middle of the pool of water inside the dwarven tunnel to the north near the zone in, right click Elaborate Peace Offering.\nThe offering sits, silent and unmoving. Nothing is happening.\nThe offering glows a soft green, as though nature itself is accepting the gift.\nWithin moments, the offering is gone. Was it sufficient? Did it go to its intended recipients?\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\n14\\. Let Wegadas know how it went 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou say, 'Hail, Wegadas'\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWegadas says, 'You're back! How did it go? Did you see them? Was it [accepted]?'\nYou say, 'I believe it was accepted. The urn glowed and then was simply gone.'\nWegadas says, 'I never thought we would have contact with such spirits of nature. I will endeavor to seek them out. Maybe we can grow in our knowledge of each other. Thank you. If you don't mind, can you let Thornel know? Our greatest druid should be alerted to this discovery.'\n15\\. Update Thornel Grayleaf on the situation 0/1 Unkempt Woods\nYou say, 'Hail, Thornel Grayleaf'\nYour task 'A Gift of Fish' has been updated.\nWhat was intended to be a gift to the adventurer became a gift for the Gihjna. There's magics in the Unkempt Woods that have yet to be revealed, and Thornel Grayleaf and Wegadas will be there for it.\nYou receive 7 copper .\nYou receive 6 silver .\nYou receive 6 gold .\nYou receive 141 platinum .\nYou have gained 1 mercenary ability point(s)!\nYou have gained 10 ability point(s)!\nYou gain experience! (1.122%) - At Level 123\nThornel Grayleaf says, 'You are telling me that you, and Wegadas, initiated contact with the Gihjna? If the story of them is true, then it is of utmost importance to nurture our relationship with them, and fight harder to save these shores from the Rallosians. Thank you for what you have done for the Elddar and the people of Tunare.'\nYou have gained 20 ability point(s)!\nYou have gained 8 mercenary ability point(s)!\nYou gain experience! (11.356%)\nYou have completed achievement: Partisan of Unkempt Woods\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141pp 6g 6s 7cp\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** NecroPost",
